Subject: [PATCH 09283/11362] Changelog: seeded repair evidence, and three
 corrections it forced

Records the session the operator held the repair default for, including the
number that decides it: 2 of 4 catastrophic cells convert outright, 2 return
their seed at ~10 minutes and one budget slot each. Reported as a conversion
rate because the +0.44 arithmetic mean describes no cell in the set.

Three corrections are written down rather than quietly superseded. The
marginal-band null was measured on a broken-nudge arm and is withdrawn. The
cross-level carry A/B never fired, so its null says nothing about carrying
knowledge. The committed +0.054 survives on its own single cell but is too
narrow to describe the lever, which closes a debt carried all session.

Also records the bound on the whole class: the goal predicate has never fired
on a real win state, verified against the corpus-artifact trap that would have
made that null uninterpretable.

